(5) peak spectrum.  CORRECTION TO MY OWN FIRST PASS: the set that carries the minor
    arcs is B_d = {a in A : a > 2d}, not A.  Measured over A the modulus-6 peak dies
    for the PRIMES too, because 3 = 3 (mod 6) is in A; but 3 leaves B_d at d >= 2.
    h_d(q) = max_{(r,q)=1} (PROD_{a in B_d} |cos(pi r a/q)|)^{1/|B_d|},  q <= 120
    modulus-4 floor 1/sqrt2 = 0.707107;  modulus-6 peak sqrt3/2 = 0.866025
========================================================================================================
